    ],
    "note": "What people call their meals depends on where they live and on their family. **Dinner** is the main meal of the day, usually in the evening, and is the more formal word (*a dinner party*). **Supper** is an evening meal, often a simple one at home (*soup for supper*); in British English it can also be a snack before bed. In parts of Britain, **tea** is the name of an early evening meal."
  },
